course: dictionary
lesson: 13773
title: Cushions in your spine
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Break the word into parts. «Inter» means between, and «vertebral» comes from vertebrae, the small bones that stack up to make your spine. So intervertebral means between the bones of the spine.
explain: «The doctor said the intervertebral disc in Sam's back was sore.» The disc is not a bone. It is the soft part that sits between two bones. Ask yourself: between what? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: «Each intervertebral disc acts like a shock absorber when you jump.» A shock absorber soaks up a bump, so the discs soak up pressure on your spine. You only need the simple idea: they are soft and sit between the bones of your back.
fact: Intervertebral means between the vertebrae, the bones of the spine.
fact: Vertebrae are the small bones that stack together to make your spine, also called your backbone.
fact: «Intervertebral discs» are soft cushions between the vertebrae.
fact: Inter means between, as in «interval» (the time between two events) and «international» (between nations).
fact: Looking at the parts of a long word, like inter- and vertebral, can help you guess what it means.
exercise: «The intervertebral disc sits in your back.» What does intervertebral mean? | Inside the heart | *Between the bones of the spine | Made of metal | Far away from the spine
exercise: «Intervertebral discs are soft cushions.» Where in the body are these discs found? | *Your back, between the bones of your spine | Your hands | Your ears | Your legs
exercise: The word starts with inter-. What does inter- mean? | *Between | Under | Above | Outside
test: «Each intervertebral disc acts like a shock absorber.» Where are these discs found? | Inside the skull | *Between the vertebrae in your back | Around the knees | In the arms
test: What is a vertebra? | A kind of muscle | A soft cushion | A part of your foot | *One of the bones that stack up to make your spine
exam: Which is the best meaning of intervertebral? | Found in the feet | *Between the bones of the spine | Very long | Full of blood
